{
 "section_summary": "This section completes most of a report on foreign students in Japan, including Chinese and colonial students, the International Students Institute, wartime controls, postwar welfare problems, statistical tables, governing documents, sources, and interviews. It then contains a May 1948 telegram about Korean-language schools in Japan and a despatch transmitting a SCAP study of Japanese educational institutions with religious affiliations. The opening portion of that study explains its methodology and begins a detailed national roster of Baptist, Catholic, Protestant, and other Christian schools.",
